{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200/multiprofile/transformer is the current best (~0.653), while image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208). The critical uncertainty is whether the image modality has any useful signal at all, or whether the poor resnet50 result reflects a fundamental lack of image informativeness. config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, ViT-L) isolates the image encoder question by swapping resnet50 for a much stronger pretrained ViT-L while keeping everything else identical to config_010. This is a single-variable comparison that directly tells us whether image carries discriminative signal. If ViT-L is also weak, we can confidently rule out image and focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinement. If ViT-L is competitive, it justifies investing in multimodal fusion experiments (e.g., config_036/037). Without this prerequisite, any multimodal result would be confounded by not knowing whether the image branch contributes or dilutes the RNA signal."
}

